<title>UK: LICHT SEES WORLD 97/98 SUGAR OUTPUT AT 123 MLN T.</title>
<headline>LICHT SEES WORLD 97/98 SUGAR OUTPUT AT 123 MLN T.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>World sugar production should fall by 700,000 tonnes raw value to 123.0 million in 1997/98 (Sept/Aug), German statistician F.O. Licht said on Thursday.</p>
<p>But consumption was expected to rise by two million tonnes which could reduce global sugar stocks by more than 1.5 million tonnes, it said.  </p>
<p>Surplus sugar stocks were expected to fall, mainly in India.</p>
<p>India could again change its status from net exporter to net importer, Licht said.</p>
<p>As a result, market fundamentals in 1997/98 could prove positive.</p>
<p>Licht gave no details for stocks or consumption in 1997/98.</p>
<p>-- Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
</text>
